<section class="how-it-works" id="how-it-works">
  <div class="hiw-header">
    <h2 class="section-title">How SATrack Works</h2>
    <p class="section-sub">From typing a word to getting smarter with every review — here's the full loop.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="hiw-steps">

    <div class="hiw-step">
      <div class="hiw-step-visual">
        <img src="/img/hiw-1-input.svg" alt="You type a word" width="320" height="180">
      </div>
      <div class="hiw-step-text">
        <span class="hiw-step-num">1</span>
        <h3>You type a word</h3>
        <p>Type any SAT vocabulary word — <strong>"perspicacious"</strong>, <strong>"ephemeral"</strong>, whatever you're studying.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="hiw-step">
      <div class="hiw-step-visual">
        <img src="/img/hiw-2-tokens.svg" alt="Word gets split into chunks" width="320" height="180">
      </div>
      <div class="hiw-step-text">
        <span class="hiw-step-num">2</span>
        <h3>The word gets split into chunks</h3>
        <p>The AI breaks <strong>"perspicacious"</strong> into smaller pieces — <strong>per</strong>, <strong>spi</strong>, <strong>ca</strong>, <strong>cious</strong>. Each piece gets a unique ID number from the model's vocabulary. This is how language models read — not as whole words, but as meaningful tokens.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="hiw-step">
      <div class="hiw-step-visual">
        <img src="/img/hiw-3-vectors.svg" alt="Tokens become numbers" width="320" height="180">
      </div>
      <div class="hiw-step-text">
        <span class="hiw-step-num">3</span>
        <h3>Each token becomes a list of numbers</h3>
        <p>Every token gets converted into a long list of numbers — like a <strong>digital fingerprint</strong> that captures its meaning. Words with similar meanings end up with similar numbers. That's how the system knows "perspicacious" is related to "sagacious" — their numbers are close together, we can, thus, represent the word as a <strong>Vector</strong>.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="hiw-step">
      <div class="hiw-step-visual">
        <img src="/img/hiw-4-index.svg" alt="Vectors stored in database" width="320" height="180">
      </div>
      <div class="hiw-step-text">
        <span class="hiw-step-num">4</span>
        <h3>Vectors get stored in a fast-lookup index</h3>
        <p>Every word's numbers are saved in a special database that's built for one thing: <strong>finding similar vectors fast</strong>. Thousands of existing entries live here, each with their own numerical fingerprint, ready to be compared.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="hiw-step">
      <div class="hiw-step-visual">
        <img src="/img/hiw-5-vectorspace.svg" alt="Words live in a 3D space" width="320" height="180">
      </div>
      <div class="hiw-step-text">
        <span class="hiw-step-num">5</span>
        <h3>Every word lives in a 3D space</h3>
        <p>Imagine every word sitting as a dot in a 3D space — <strong>words with similar meanings cluster together</strong>. "Perspicacious" lands near "sagacious" and "shrewd", while "ephemeral" sits far away in its own neighborhood.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="hiw-step">
      <div class="hiw-step-visual">
        <img src="/img/hiw-6-similarity.svg" alt="Dot product finds nearest neighbors" width="320" height="180">
      </div>
      <div class="hiw-step-text">
        <span class="hiw-step-num">6</span>
        <h3>A math operation finds the nearest neighbors</h3>
        <p>The system multiplies your word's numbers against every stored word's numbers — a <strong>dot product</strong>. The higher the result, the closer the two words sit in the space. The three closest dots are your word's nearest neighbors.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="hiw-step">
      <div class="hiw-step-visual">
        <img src="/img/hiw-7-search.svg" alt="Best matches extracted" width="320" height="180">
      </div>
      <div class="hiw-step-text">
        <span class="hiw-step-num">7</span>
        <h3>The best matches become style references</h3>
        <p>The top 3 nearest neighbors get pulled out of the space. These aren't just similar words — they're <strong>entries that were already written well</strong>. The AI uses them as a style guide to match the tone, format, and quality of what worked before.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="hiw-step">
      <div class="hiw-step-visual">
        <img src="/img/hiw-8-generate.svg" alt="AI generates the entry" width="320" height="180">
      </div>
      <div class="hiw-step-text">
        <span class="hiw-step-num">8</span>
        <h3>AI writes the entry</h3>
        <p>Using the style references as a guide, the AI writes a <strong>mnemonic</strong>, a <strong>picture story</strong>, and an <strong>example sentence</strong>. It also looks at past feedback — if users have been saying mnemonics are too long, it adjusts.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="hiw-step">
      <div class="hiw-step-visual">
        <img src="/img/hiw-9-quality.svg" alt="Quality check" width="320" height="180">
      </div>
      <div class="hiw-step-text">
        <span class="hiw-step-num">9</span>
        <h3>Quality is verified</h3>
        <p>Before you see the entry, it goes through two checks: a <strong>rule check</strong> (does the definition exist? does the sentence actually use the word?) and an <strong>AI judge</strong> (is the mnemonic clever? is the picture vivid?). Only entries that pass both make it through.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="hiw-step">
      <div class="hiw-step-visual">
        <img src="/img/hiw-10-entry.svg" alt="You get a polished entry" width="320" height="180">
      </div>
      <div class="hiw-step-text">
        <span class="hiw-step-num">10</span>
        <h3>You get a polished entry</h3>
        <p>A complete vocabulary card: pronunciation, definition, mnemonic, picture story, other forms, and a sentence. <strong>Copy it, add it to flashcards, or save it to a list.</strong></p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="hiw-step">
      <div class="hiw-step-visual">
        <img src="/img/hiw-11-feedback.svg" alt="Feedback makes it smarter" width="320" height="180">
      </div>
      <div class="hiw-step-text">
        <span class="hiw-step-num">11</span>
        <h3>Your feedback makes it smarter</h3>
        <p>Rate each entry from 1–10. The system tracks what users love (vivid stories? clever mnemonics?) and what falls flat. <strong>Every rating shapes future generations</strong> — so SATrack literally gets better the more people use it.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

  </div>
</section>

